      "message": "feat(ui): the shell runs in a browser - eframe web runner, awaited GPU start-up (#31 rung 3)\n\nThe browser shell is egui_app/shell_web.rs (wasm32 only): an eframe::App\nover a <canvas> that runs the same shell::shell_layout frame and the same\n3D pass as the native window, started from the page through the exported\ncamcraft_start(canvas_id). eframe awaits the adapter, device and surface;\na refusal is said on the page (#camcraft-status) and in the console,\nnever a panic.\n\n- view_pass.rs: the scene upload gate, target sizing, View3D + traced\n  stock pass and the repaint law, moved unchanged out of the native frame\n  so both shells share them.\n- The blocking GPU waits get awaited twins: TracePass::new_async,\n  Composite::new_async, StockEye::new_async, headless_gpu::device_async.\n  The blocking forms are thin native-only wrappers; pollster is now a\n  native-only dependency. The native-only trace readback moved to\n  trace/readback.rs.\n- web/index.html and web/wasi_shim.js: the page, and the nine\n  wasi_snapshot_preview1 imports flecs' libc asks for, wired by an\n  import map.\n- web/build-app-wasm.sh links the UI as a cdylib (cargo rustc\n  --crate-type, manifest unchanged), runs the wasm-bindgen CLI pinned by\n  Cargo.lock and lays out target/web; it fails if the module asks for a\n  WASI import the shim does not answer.\n\nProved in headless Chrome (WebGL2 through SwiftShader): the module\ninstantiates, the first frame draws, a click on the ribbon opens the\nStock page. The WebGPU path was not exercised.\n\nRefs #31\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
