      "message": "fix(ui): browser diagnostics reach the console; shim answers match its comments (#31 review)\n\nReview findings on PR #847:\n- crate::diag is the UI crate's one diagnostics seam: diag_warn! and\n  diag_info! print to stderr/stdout natively and to the page console on\n  wasm32, where std drops both streams. The stock eye's fall-back to the\n  CPU march, the file dialog's \"cancelled\" note and the other direct\n  prints in browser-compiled UI code go through it; a law test fails on\n  a direct print outside the seam.\n- wasi_shim.js: poll_oneoff succeeds at once, reports clock\n  subscriptions as elapsed and says the skipped wait in the console\n  (it answered ENOSYS under a comment that promised a return). Unknown\n  clock ids and closed descriptors answer a named errno with a console\n  warning. The functions outside the module's nine imports are removed.\n- build-app-wasm.sh: the missing-imports message prints under pipefail;\n  the wasm-bindgen install is announced before it runs and\n  CAMCRAFT_WASM_NO_INSTALL=1 refuses it with instructions.\n- view_pass::target_extent holds the pixel ratio to 0.1..=8 itself, so\n  the first browser target is clamped like every later frame.\n\nRefs #31\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
